    "payload": {
      "arguments": {
        "content": "# Product Comparison Report\n\nI compared Atlas, Birch, and Cedar across price, project limit, retention, and export format.\n\n## Comparison table\n\n| Product | Price | Project limit | Retention | Export |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Atlas | 120 USD | 40 projects | 7 days | CSV |\n| Birch | 180 USD | 75 projects | 14 days | JSON |\n| Cedar | 240 USD | 90 projects | 30 days | XML |\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**Cedar** is the best choice if you want the most generous limits and longest retention, and it also supports XML export. **Atlas** is the lowest-cost option, but it has the smallest limits and shortest retention. **Birch** is a middle ground on price and capability.\n\n## Sources\n\n- Atlas: http://127.0.0.1:56984/atlas — \"Price 120 USD; limit 40 projects; retention 7 days; export CSV.\"\n- Birch: http://127.0.0.1:56984/birch — \"Price 180 USD; limit 75 projects; retention 14 days; export JSON.\"\n- Cedar: http://127.0.0.1:56984/cedar — \"Price 240 USD; limit 90 projects; retention 30 days; export XML.\"\n",
        "media_type": "text/markdown",
        "name": "report.md"
      },
